OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Tue 1 Dec to Thu 10 Dec
OL,6,FHigh pressure may become quite
OL,7,Fdominant across the UK through this
OL,8,Fperiod. Weather systems will continue
OL,9,Fto try and push eastwards across the
OL,10,FUK, but will tend to weaken or even
OL,11,Fstall as they encounter the high
OL,12,Fpressure. So, whilst there may be
OL,13,Fquite a lot of dry weather through
OL,14,Fthis period, further spells of rain or
OL,15,Fshowers are likely at times, which may
OL,16,Fbe heavy in places, with some hill
OL,17,Fsnow possible, especially in the
OL,18,Fnorth. With high pressure possibly
OL,19,Flargely in charge, frost and fog may
OL,20,Fbe more prevalent than usual.
OL,21,FTemperatures are likely to be variable
OL,22,Fthrough the period, but overall close
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,23,Fto normal. Some colder interludes are
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
OL,24,Fpossible, especially if northerly or
OL,25,Feasterly flows develop, these
OL,26,Fdependent on the location of high
